        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Revise scrollbar colors in CSS guide]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46113</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46113"/>
        <updated>2026-10-12T14:34:33.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Updated scrollbar styling example with new colors that have sufficient contrast.</p>
<p dir="auto">An A11Y team was looking at this page:</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Scrollbars_styling" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Scrollbars_styling</a></p>
<p dir="auto">and noted the red on yellow isn't meeting 1.4.11 contrast requirements of 3 to 1.</p>
<p dir="auto">They suggested color combo that work (that are interesting):</p>
<p dir="auto">Teal<br>
thumb #0B4F4A<br>
track #5F9E98<br>
background #FFFFFF</p>
<p dir="auto">Purple<br>
thumb #4B0082<br>
track #9E7FD0<br>
background #FFFFFF</p>]]></content>
