    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Keyboard accessible: note that screen readers can replace key events with click]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46079</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46079"/>
        <updated>2026-10-09T17:09:53.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75755802?u=232cfdb37381645af6e176bf8b8b2a4d1d3a3495&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Adds a paragraph to "Focusable elements should have interactive semantics" on the Keyboard accessible guide: in browse mode, some screen readers intercept <kbd>Enter</kbd> and <kbd>Space</kbd> and activate the element with a <code class="notranslate">click</code> event, so <code class="notranslate">keydown</code> and <code class="notranslate">keyup</code> handlers never run. Touch screen readers fire <code class="notranslate">click</code> on double tap. The paragraph tells readers to handle <code class="notranslate">click</code> as well, or use a native <code class="notranslate">&lt;button&gt;</code>. Also adds the <code class="notranslate">click</code> event to the section's "See also" list and fixes "event handlers keyboard events" to "event handlers for keyboard events".</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The section only recommends keyboard event handlers. A custom control built that way does nothing for an NVDA user in browse mode, which is the case reported in the issue.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>NVDA discussion of the behavior: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="286453272" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/nvaccess/nvda/issues/7898" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/nvaccess/nvda/issues/7898/hovercard" href="https://github.com/nvaccess/nvda/issues/7898">nvaccess/nvda#7898</a></li>
<li>Checked in Chromium: a focused <code class="notranslate">&lt;button&gt;</code> fires <code class="notranslate">click</code> on both Enter and Space; a focused <code class="notranslate">&lt;div tabindex="0"&gt;</code> gets only <code class="notranslate">keydown</code> and <code class="notranslate">keyup</code>.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">markdownlint-cli2</code> and <code class="notranslate">prettier -c</code> pass on the file.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #37887.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2821371672" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37887" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/37887/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37887">#37887</a></p>]]></content>
